            style="font-size: 9px; color: rgb(124, 122, 148); margin-top: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
          >
            authors
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          style="background: rgb(30, 32, 52); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px; cursor: default;"
        >
          <div
            style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(76, 184, 136); line-height: 1.1;"
          >
            17
          </div>
          <div
            style="font-size: 10px; color: rgb(150, 148, 172); margin-top: 1px;"
          >
            Scans
          </div>
          <div
            style="font-size: 9px; color: rgb(124, 122, 148); margin-top: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
          >
            today
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          style="background: rgb(30, 32, 52); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px; cursor: default;"
        >
          <div
            style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(228, 184, 104); line-height: 1.1;"
          >
            2,210
          </div>
          <div
            style="font-size: 10px; color: rgb(150, 148, 172); margin-top: 1px;"
          >
            Pages
          </div>
          <div
            style="font-size: 9px; color: rgb(124, 122, 148); margin-top: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
          >
            cached
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      style="position: fixed; inset: 0px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; z-index: 100;"
    >
      <div
        style="width: min(640px, 92vw); background: rgb(34, 36, 56); border: 1px solid rgb(58, 60, 86); border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; color: rgb(236, 234, 244); max-height: 85vh; overflow-y: auto;"
      >
        <div
          style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          Run Data Hygiene?
        </div>
        <div
          style="font-size: 13px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-bottom: 14px;"
        >
          This will fan the following 11 jobs across every configured library, in order. Re-running is idempotent — re-runs are near-no-ops once everything is clean.
        </div>
        <ol
          style="padding-left: 22px; margin: 0px 0px 18px;"
        >
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              1. Empty author + series cleanup
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Removes authors with 0 books (preserving your allowlist) and series with no members.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              2. Hardcover identifier backfill
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              For books with hardcover_id, stamps any missing Goodreads / OpenLibrary / Google Books IDs from Hardcover's mapping table.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              3. Phase-2 author goodreads_id backfill
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Resolves authors whose books now carry a goodreads_id, looking up the author's id via reverse-lookup.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              4. Book deduplication
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Merges book rows sharing any non-null identifier (Goodreads / Hardcover / ISBN / ASIN / Audible) plus same-series-position duplicates.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              5. Series consolidation
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Collapses series under the same author whose names canonicalize to the same form ('Mistborn' vs 'The Mistborn Saga').
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              6. ABS author cross-stamp
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Copies goodreads_id / hardcover_id / etc. from enriched ebook authors to ABS authors with the same name.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              7. Orphan author retrolink
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              For every per-library author row missing an author_links entry (e.g. stub rows inserted by the v2.12.1 mirror or other paths that bypassed the identity hook), creates or reuses the right \`persons\` row so it joins the cross-library identity graph.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              8. Cross-library person backfill
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Walks every multi-link person; mirrors NULL source IDs across linked siblings (Amazon/Goodreads/Hardcover/etc.), audit-logs ebook-wins conflict resolution, backfills \`persons.bio\` from any non-null sibling, clears broken book-cover-as-author-photo URLs, and recomputes link_confidence flags so Author Triage stays accurate.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              9. Consolidate persons by shared source ID
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Finds distinct \`persons\` rows that share a (source, source_id) via their linked author rows and merges them into one (winner = lowest person_id). Backfills slice 03's runtime ID-consolidation across pre-existing data so the split-person gap (Heinlein vs Heinlein, A.) closes in one pass. Audit-logged to \`person_merges\`; idempotent.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              10. Prune orphan author_links
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Drops global \`author_links\` rows whose per-library author no longer exists (cross-file FK can't cascade automatically). Also removes any \`persons\` rows that become unreferenced.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              11. Image URL health check
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Substring-clears author images under \`/books/\` (book-cover-as-photo regression — historically the John-Birmingham row) or containing \`nophoto\` (Goodreads placeholders), then HEAD-verifies remaining populated rows and clears any non-200. Local-clear-only — the next discovery scan refills the slot via the rank-aware mirror.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              12. Soft-delete retention sweep
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Filesystem-only. Walks each library's .seshat-replaced/&lt;ts&gt;/ folders and purges anything older than the active-replacement retention window (default 30 days). Idempotent — a near-no-op once steady state is reached.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li
            style="margin-bottom: 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(236, 234, 244);"
            >
              13. Non-roster author cleanup
            </div>
            <div
              style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); margin-top: 2px;"
            >
              Removes authors a source scan created that are neither on your allow list nor own a book in the library, plus the unowned books left with no contributor. Repairs the fallout: re-points dangling series links, and renumbers any book that lost its primary author. Library (Calibre/ABS) authors are never touched, and owned books can't lose a byline. Inert unless this install ran a source scan before v3.10.0.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <div
          style="font-size: 11px; color: rgb(214, 212, 224); background: rgb(30, 32, 52); padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 14px;"
        >
          <b>
            Universal rules
          </b>
          : hidden items skipped where applicable, \`authors_allowed\` preserved by name, Hardcover calls reuse the existing 1s rate limit.
        </div>
        <div
          style="display: flex; gap: 8px; justify-content: flex-end;"
        >
          <button
            style="padding: 7px 14px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 13px; background: rgb(42, 44, 66); color: rgb(214, 212, 224); border: 1px solid rgb(58, 60, 86); cursor: pointer;"
          >
            Cancel
          </button>
          <button
            style="padding: 7px 14px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; background: rgb(228, 184, 104); color: rgb(26, 28, 48); border: 1px solid rgb(228, 184, 104); cursor: pointer; opacity: 1; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;"
          >
            Run Hygiene
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocumentFragment>
`;

